	<TEXT>
		<Tag>TXT_KEY_LEADER_CHIANG_CHING_KUO_PEDIA</Tag>
		<English>Chiang Ching-kuo was a pivotal leader in Taiwan's modern history, renowned for initiating the "Ten Major Construction Projects" that powered Taiwan's industrial and economic miracle. In his later years, he ended martial law, opening the path for Taiwan's flourishing democracy.</English>
